values ('f4a5b6c7-8d9e-4f39-8c89-9a0b1c2d3e29', 'religion-and-society', 'Religion and Society', 'Religion and Society examines how religious ideas, practices, institutions, communities, and identities shape social life, and how social forces reshape religion. The course connects sociology of religion, religious studies, politics, law, race and gender studies, migration studies, media studies, ethics, public policy, and global affairs. Students learn to analyze religion as a lived and public phenomenon using theory, empirical evidence, case studies, and current data.');

